  situation: 'In a village near Lagdo, which has grown from 50 to more than 200 families, two elders debate. Mallam Bello says: "The land of each family is getting smaller and the soil is tired; soon there will be hunger and conflict!" Madame Fanta, head of the women\'s farming cooperative, answers: "More people means more hands and more minds; this pressure will push our children to irrigate from the lake and use better seeds!" A young man listening asks: "Who is right, and are these only the opinions of two elders?"',
